# KONSTRIVO PRO Web Environment Variables
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.konstrivo.tn/api/v1
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCALE=fr

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner admin — local authority gate (R-001).
# SECURITY WARNING (static export): with `output: 'export'` these values ARE
# embedded into the client bundle. The credential is NOT a secret — it is a
# salted PBKDF2 hash replacing plaintext storage. Protection is CLIENT-SIDE
# ONLY (local dashboard gate), NOT server-side authentication.
# NEVER place a real password here or in any committed file.
# Format / generator command: see root `.env.example` (or run
#   node generate-admin.js YOUR_STRONG_PASSWORD  from the project root).
# Placeholders below are intentionally INVALID -> login FAILS CLOSED until you
# set real values in your local untracked `.env` / `.env.local`.
#
# KEY-NAMING NOTE: keys MUST keep the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix or Next.js will not
# inline them into the client bundle (the gate would always fail closed).
# The unprefixed ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD_CREDENTIAL names belong to the
# Android root `.env`, not here. (Keys were corrected 2026-09-09 — the previous
# EMAIL/PASSWORD names matched nothing in web/src/app/page.tsx.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_EMAIL=example@example.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_CREDENTIAL=REPLACE_WITH_GENERATED_CREDENTIAL
